{"name":"Butternut Squash","hex":"#fc7604","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"butternut squash","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vase-shaped orange-fleshed hard winter squash, a cultivar of Cucurbita moschata."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/butternut_squash"}],"entries":[{"title":"Butternut squash","blocks":[{"text":"Butternut squash, known in Australia and New Zealand as butternut pumpkin or gramma, is a type of winter squash that grows on a vine. It has a sweet, nutty taste, when cooked, similar to that of a pumpkin. It has tan-yellow skin and orange fleshy pulp with a compartment of seeds in the blossom end. When ripening, the flesh turns increasingly deep orange due to its rich content of beta-carotene, a provitamin A compound."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Cucurbita_moschata_Butternut_2012_G2.jpg/330px-Cucurbita_moschata_Butternut_2012_G2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butternut_squash","wikidata":"Q4169287"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Butternut_Developpment.jpg/500px-Butternut_Developpment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Butternut_Developpment.jpg/1280px-Butternut_Developpment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Butternut_Developpment.jpg/500px-Butternut_Developpment.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stages of development of butternut squash","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AButternut_Developpment.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Cucurbita_moschata_%27Butternut%27_3.jpg/500px-Cucurbita_moschata_%27Butternut%27_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki